            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I started implementing fix for something I called \"inconsitent behavior of color column\", but after some investigation I'm not sure what expected behavior should be. \r\n\r\nHere are my notes on this issue mentioned in previous comment:\r\n> `colorcolumn` looks/behaves inconsistently with `wrapcolumn`\r\n\r\nmini glossary (how I understand different terms):\r\n\r\n> **_line_** / **_buffer line_** - a logical line of text in the buffer/file, terminated by `\\n`. What line numbers refer to.\r\n>\r\n> **_screen line_** - a single row of characters as rendered on screen. One buffer line may occupy multiple screen lines when wrap is enabled.\r\n>\r\n> **_short line_** - a line shorter than the value of `colorcolumn`\r\n> **_long line_** - a line longer than the value of `colorcolumn`\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n**Problem:**\r\n`colorcolumn` behaves differently for short and long lines.\r\n- **short and empty lines:** the column of the screen line is colored\r\n- **long lines:** the column of the buffer line is colored\r\n\r\nIt's confusing when `wrapcolumn` is introduced - column colors look random (see screenshot).\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2500\" height=\"1600\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbe61854-0f72-480d-8a8a-87a3fa96b756\" />\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\nIt turns out this behavior is consistent with how `colorcolumn` acts when `wrap` is set but `wrapcolumn` isn't being used or implemented (see GIF showcase). It's not that noticeable when we use a single `colorcolumn` value and a relatively wide terminal window.\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2500\" height=\"1600\" alt=\"demo\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a3c44c4-55c9-47bf-b7eb-8c658907f1e9\" />\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior:**\r\n`colorcolumn` should be marked only on the screen line (my personal preference) and not visible when window is narrower.\r\n\r\nBut there are also voices suggesting that coloring the buffer line is the preferred way (see related issues).\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n**Conclusion:**\r\nI wouldn't call the behavior of `colorcolumn` after introducing `wrapcolumn` a regression. But there is a need for a consistent definition of how Neovim should behave in these situations (keeping it as it is now, creating an option to define this behavior, coloring the column only in screen lines, or something else).\r\n\r\n**There are some related issues and reports:**\r\n- #24600 \r\n- https://github.com/vim/vim/issues/18726\r\n",
